{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Cn3Djm3jX8K14ZDjogHkCv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All acceptance criteria have been verified and pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**File created:** `cmd/sponge/main.go`\n\n**PRD coverage (prd007-sponge R1-R5):**\n\n- **R1 (Core soak-before-write):** Reads all stdin into a dynamically grown buffer starting at 8192 bytes. Spills to temp file when memory threshold is exceeded. Temp file created in TMPDIR or system temp dir with \"sponge\" prefix. Cleanup handler registered for SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP.\n\n- **R2 (Output file handling):** Atomic rename via `os.Rename`. Cross-device fallback via `isCrossDeviceError` check and `io.Copy`. File mode preservation via `os.Lstat` (not `os.Stat`). New files get mode 0666 masked by umask.\n\n- **R3 (Append mode):** `-a` flag prepends original file content before stdin content. When output file doesn't exist, behaves as default mode.\n\n- **R4 (Passthrough mode):** No output filename writes buffered stdin to stdout. Handles both in-memory buffer and temp-file-spill cases.\n\n- **R5 (Exit codes):** Exit 0 on success, exit 1 with descriptive stderr message on any failure. Temp file cleaned up on all exit paths.\n\n**Design decisions followed:** D1 (manual flag parsing from cmd/cat), D2 (SIGPIPE handling pattern), D3 (os.CreateTemp with TMPDIR), D4 (os.Rename with cross-device fallback), D5 (os.Lstat for output path)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":112985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4436eefb-e1ea-49fc-984f-7fffcc0bc527","uuid":"92fe435a-06d7-4fab-acd6-f887c0eff90d"}
